{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791046365,"nonce":"Gi1O0B3YJO7M1cl21nDozqi+UuQ=","title":"ZynML: awaiting an extern def host bridge segfaults on a null promise load","message":"In ZynML, a host bridge declared directly and awaited,\n\n    extern def __zyntax_async_set_timeout(ms: i64)\n    ...\n    await __zyntax_async_set_timeout(30)\n\nsegfaults: the JIT code loads a promise {state_machine, poll_fn} from address 0 and calls through it. The await appears to take the generic path for awaiting another async function rather than the host-bridge park, because the callee reaches lowering as an extern function, not as a Symbol callee carrying the __zyntax_async_ prefix that selects the park. The builtin alias route (sleep -\u003e __zyntax_async_set_timeout) works and is what caribou uses.\n\nExpected: an await whose callee is a host bridge parks on the bridge's future however the bridge was declared, or the declaration is refused with a diagnostic naming what to use instead; never a null call.\n\nReported by the caribou session (cross-language runtime work); not reproduced here yet.","files":null}]}